Package: csectionparadoxbd
Type: ResearchCompendium
Title: Identification Diagnostics for C-Section Causal Inference on Bangladesh DHS Data
Version: 1.0.0
Date: 2026-05-23
Authors@R:
    person("Mukarram", "Hosain",
           email = "moccaram@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description:
    A reproducible research compendium for the analysis described in
    docs/BRIEF.md. The repository contains the full pipeline used to
    estimate the effect of C-section delivery on under-24-month child
    mortality in Bangladesh across DHS waves 2004, 2011, 2017-18, and
    2022 — and the diagnostic chain that demonstrates why the resulting
    point estimate does not warrant a causal interpretation. The
    pipeline includes descriptive evidence of Bangladesh's
    supply-constrained to demand-driven C-section regime transition,
    spatial models using Malaria Atlas Project travel-time instruments,
    a recursive bivariate probit (RBVP) with cluster-bootstrap
    inference, three formal identification diagnostics (cross-instrument
    placebo, Wooldridge-style endogeneity test via 2SRI, copula
    sensitivity), and a modern-inference layer (E-value, sensemakr,
    simplified Acerenza inequalities, Chow test).
